rem Permutation of 3-smooth Numbers
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=462

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option N integer = 1000000000000000000

rem 2^a 3^b is cell (b, a) of a Young
rem diagram: row b holds the a with
rem 2^a <= N / 3^b. Valid orders are
rem its standard tableaux, counted by
rem the hook-length formula.
B = (0 to 40) copy
B = B ((3 ** B at most N) indices)
Q = N // (3 ** B)
W = 2 ** (0 to 62) copy
L = (Q W outer at least) count rank 1
C = (0 till (L first)) copy
H = (C L outer less) count rank 1
R = (0 till L len) copy
Hk = ((L - R - 1) C outer -) + H
Hk = (L C outer greater) choose Hk 1
Dn = (Hk reduce *) reduce *
F = (1 to (L sum)) reduce * // Dn
rem Ten decimals, rounded exactly.
E = (F text) len - 1
Rd = (F * 10 ** 12 // 10 ** E + 5) // 10
Ld = Rd text
Answer = Ld (0 till 1) + "."
Answer += Ld (1 till 11) + "e"
Answer += E text
Answer print
